\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"00a8a97e0bafb5980c4f3c921a7e13c4a61f38d1afcde6d254936aec660665c1","event_uuid":"ac9715fc-b484-4c75-9235-1a0ced1ea5d8","position":{"commit_sha":"a33e30ad45bb4a4eaba1a47804af02de31c6f466","position":"1786652466482306001-ac9715fc-b484-4c75-9235-1a0ced1ea5d8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"be5fb7e19b2253e0ca266ebf829a042facd6d9a17c18731805a046107c2d2f8a","event_uuid":"92412372-cfff-4c0c-84a4-bff87daf6eec","position":{"commit_sha":"0e77f612287e4a94cab7739e88e0d744d28772f0","position":"1786653186368467001-92412372-cfff-4c0c-84a4-bff87daf6eec"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"93549825e3f3f95b9e7d547dfead050e93e22032dc216acf10696e8a338c965e","event_uuid":"f8af06c4-53a3-478b-9c2f-516f2ff13f88","position":{"commit_sha":"158f1d971e7fbafc841217f9f1f17fe887f51531","position":"1786653192061660001-f8af06c4-53a3-478b-9c2f-516f2ff13f88"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-227_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6f8df6b5-44f6-4ea4-b224-1eac4c95b0a7","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"CHECKPOINT — peak-window pause (operator-ordered 5-11am PT). NOT STARTED beyond planning.\n\nSTATE: plan written into the description and PASSED review-plan; ticket claimed/in_progress. ZERO code or docs edits made — nothing is staged, committed, or pushed for this ticket. The worktree ../operator-batch2 (branch operator-batch2) is clean at commit e57ca52587, which belongs to rasbora, not to this ticket.\n\nRESUME PLAN, unchanged from the description: add the standing rule to AGENTS.md as one bullet plus a narrowed clause on the existing 'The gate' bullet (which today reads 'comment recheck if it is a flake'); reconcile CONTRIBUTING.md section 6's 'Verified -1 but the failure looks transient/flaky' bullet so it splits environmental faults from test nondeterminism; add tests/unit/test_flaky_test_guidance.py pinning both the new rule and the ABSENCE of the old retry-until-green licence.\n\nTwo facts confirmed during planning, worth not re-deriving: the /rebar-debug skill lives at examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md, and no existing test pins the 'recheck if it is a flake' wording in either AGENTS.md or CONTRIBUTING.md, so narrowing them breaks nothing. docs/dependency-advisory-runbook.md already states the same shape for its own gate and is consistent, so it needs no edit.\n\nIronic and worth noting on resume: this session's own CI selection hit the hammerkop order-dependent decline-test flake, which is precisely the class this ticket's rule says to debug rather than retry.","timestamp":1786622295595975001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed as Gerrit change 1734 (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1), merged to gerrit/main as cecc72b27f.\n\nAGENTS.md now states the rule — an intermittently failing test is a bug to root-cause via /rebar-debug, fix the class not the run, with the three-part rationale in one sentence — and reserves recheck for provably environmental faults with the reasoning stated in the comment. CONTRIBUTING.md section 6 stays the CI-triage home and splits the two cases to opposite remedies instead of contradicting it. The two cross-link.\n\nThe test pins both halves; the second is the load-bearing one, asserting the old retry-until-green licence is ABSENT from both files. Verified by restoring the AGENTS.md sentence and watching it fail.\n\nNote on how this ticket was landed: it was originally stacked on 1731, which is parked behind a macOS xdist worker-crash flake (bug 0078-fa3e). Rather than submit the stack top and drag an ungated ancestor onto main, the stack was re-parented so this change sits directly on main. That ordering discipline is the same concern as the WIP rule in e30d-b5e7-f4de-4f91.\n\nThe rule was also exercised on itself during this batch: change 1731 took two Verified -1s from the same crashed worker on the same macOS cell. It was triaged, filed as a bug with evidence, and NOT rechecked a third time.","timestamp":1786652450265852001}],"created_at":1786616470523047001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a0fd1931-b1ec-4381-87b8-188b444163be","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"36e5-e213-02d5-42b8"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nOperator directive (verbatim, 2026-08-13): 'add standing guidance for the project: flaky tests get debugged using rebar-debug, not retried until they pass. a flaky CI pipeline is a failure that slows development, wastes tokens, and decreases our trust in CI as a regression oracle.'\n\nTonight's evidence: the order-dependent leaked-logger flake (future-fibroid-hammerkop) cost four `Verified -1`s across changes 1715/1716/1717/1720, multiple recheck cycles, and hours of queued rebases before it was root-caused (deterministic RED via a two-file pytest invocation) and fixed class-wide in change 1721. Root-causing it once was cheaper than every recheck combined.\n\nThe guidance today points the other way. `AGENTS.md` says \"A `Verified -1` is a CI failure (open the run; comment `recheck` if it is a flake)\", and `CONTRIBUTING.md` §6 says \"**`Verified -1` but the failure looks transient/flaky.** Comment **`recheck`** to re-run CI on the same patchset.\" Both read as licence to retry a nondeterministic test until it passes. Adding the new rule without narrowing these two would leave the repo self-contradicting.\n\n## Approach\nOne authoritative wording in `AGENTS.md` (the canonical agent guidance, read by every harness); the two existing recheck lines are narrowed to point at it rather than restate it.\n\n1. **The rule, in `AGENTS.md`** — replace the parenthetical on the existing \"The gate\" bullet and add ONE sibling bullet in the same Git-workflow list, in that list's bolded-lead style. It must carry three things and no more: (a) a test that fails intermittently is a **bug to root-cause**, not a retry — debug it with the `/rebar-debug` workflow (hypothesis-driven, isolated worktree, deterministic RED before any fix) and fix the class, not the instance; (b) the one-sentence rationale — a flaky pipeline slows development, wastes tokens, and erodes CI as a regression oracle; (c) the narrow carve-out — `recheck` is for **provably environmental** faults (a TLS/promisor cert flake, a missing CI dispatch, a runner outage) and the recheck comment must state that reasoning. AGENTS.md's keep-it-lean rule caps this at the bullet plus the one-clause edit above it.\n2. **Reconcile `CONTRIBUTING.md` §6** — rewrite the \"`Verified -1` but the failure looks transient/flaky\" bullet so it splits the two cases explicitly: an environmental fault is recheckable with stated reasoning; a nondeterministic **test** is a bug and gets debugged, with a pointer to the AGENTS.md rule. The adjacent \"CI didn't run / no run appeared\" bullet is already an environmental case and stays as-is — it is the carve-out's worked example, so it is left alone deliberately rather than overlooked.\n3. **Cross-link, don't duplicate** — `docs/dependency-advisory-runbook.md` already states the same shape for its own gate (\"Only a DB-unreachable failure is recheckable. `recheck` can NEVER clear a real finding\"); it is consistent with the new rule and needs no edit. No new doc is created: `CONTRIBUTING.md` §6 remains the CI-triage home and now points at the rule instead of contradicting it.\n\n**Out of scope.** No change to the `recheck` trigger mechanism, the review bot, or `gerrit-verify.yaml` — this ticket changes guidance only. No quarantine/auto-retry tooling is added; the directive is explicitly that flakes are debugged, so building a retry facility would contradict it.\n\n## Scope\n- `AGENTS.md` — the rule bullet plus the narrowed clause on the existing \"The gate\" bullet.\n- `CONTRIBUTING.md` — §6's transient/flaky bullet, reconciled and cross-linked.\n- `tests/unit/test_flaky_test_guidance.py` — new; pins the rule and the reconciliation.\n\n## Testing\nThis is guidance, so the testable behavior is that the rule is present AND that the old retry-until-green licence is gone — the second half is what a plain \"text exists\" test would miss.\n- **Happy path:** a new `tests/unit/test_flaky_test_guidance.py` asserts `AGENTS.md` carries the rule's load-bearing phrases (intermittent failure is a bug to root-cause, the `/rebar-debug` pointer, the three-part rationale, and the environmental-only carve-out) and that `CONTRIBUTING.md` §6 names both branches.\n- **Failure/regression path:** the same test asserts the **contradiction is gone** — neither file still tells a reader to `recheck` because a failure \"looks transient/flaky\" without qualifying it as environmental. Verified by restoring the old sentence locally and watching the test fail before reverting.\n- **Gates:** `make lint`, `make typecheck`, the `check_*` gates, generator no-diff, and the CI unit selection (`test_codex_agent_guidance.py` and `test_agents_claim_assignee_guidance.py` already pin other AGENTS.md content, so they prove the edit did not disturb neighbouring guidance).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `AGENTS.md` carries the rule as concise agent guidance with the rationale compressed to one sentence naming all three costs (slows development, wastes tokens, erodes CI as a regression oracle).\n- [x] The guidance names the deterministic-reproduction expectation via the `/rebar-debug` workflow and the narrow legitimate-recheck carve-out (provably environmental faults, reasoning stated in the recheck comment).\n- [x] `CONTRIBUTING.md` §6 no longer offers `recheck` for a failure that merely \"looks transient/flaky\", and cross-links the AGENTS.md rule instead of restating it; `AGENTS.md`'s own \"`recheck` if it is a flake\" clause is narrowed the same way.\n- [x] `tests/unit/test_flaky_test_guidance.py` pins both the new rule and the absence of the old licence, and passes; `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the CI unit selection are green.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"AGENTS.md","reason":"the authoritative rule plus the narrowed recheck clause"},{"path":"CONTRIBUTING.md","reason":"reconcile the CI -1 triage bullet with the rule"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_flaky_test_guidance.py","reason":"pin the rule and the absence of the old retry licence"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","36e5-e213-02d5-42b8"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"92412372-cfff-4c0c-84a4-bff87daf6eec","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"9b79-56ba-0d16-4c49","ticket_type":"task","title":"Guidance: flaky tests get debugged, not retried","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["4cd8b5b2-4b3f-4298-aed2-2712f93ae0bd","82808bd3-05e8-43a3-964b-afdb14c0e59a","743d5857-e065-4633-a18e-b034b9fe8151","e360d234-7813-439e-97e5-6eabce4ae95a","6daaa9c3-0295-4ac8-a248-5f61deac4be2","f7e89c59-37f5-48c8-8595-5cc9e7c77a18","527ea19f-03ca-4f21-adf8-8f0922856dec","a0fd1931-b1ec-4381-87b8-188b444163be","aa092775-60b8-4435-856f-101c88533579","ac9715fc-b484-4c75-9235-1a0ced1ea5d8","92412372-cfff-4c0c-84a4-bff87daf6eec","f8af06c4-53a3-478b-9c2f-516f2ff13f88"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659639902985001,"uuid":"b69272d4-3f46-40dc-9e91-f8ae3961a124"}